{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_19297ec6ba05c9f5cfc3414eadc801aea4623d280ececd53e8237b74caf2ed1f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2f4179de471f21b54d475dc7b38a557a830b70394c0c4b410079d91ce0a4fba3"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"Model-generated commands execute in a sandbox; the default `--sandbox-backend auto` prefers Apple's container runtime on Apple silicon, falls back to Docker-backed OCI, and fails closed if no sandbox engine is ready rather than running on the host.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3bac6df4dc881f94c3b8ee6d4e9a4e92b6f4b8eb0d84314c6974fab02dde376d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d7f2251affe89034d0b4e991b998b8792d8786ffd248753ca899afde793b6ec","slc_8f0e1b2f25fb34b4e6b85f227777fb3324e09430d50bd19ed0359395f4ff1aea"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"Findings must be execution-grounded: a finding is upgraded only when a cited local command exercises the vulnerable path, with statuses like confirmed-differential, confirmed-executable, suspected, and refuted.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3dfb7167b74b95d3a06e253d2b9dd2dba6705134f181672214d0b221ef575e40","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f3b75e1ab44f3f465232e91dd9a40bf34e8bec4e81d4757fcd04a42b868f56f","slc_aba5918a28d759498930ee30009319dd90838601b97e4015622d84fc0cda20b4"],"source_ids":["src_57c7248325f15442a1f02a4c54eff8f9","src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The framework is deliberately stack-agnostic: it encodes no Solidity, ZK, Rust, Go, or crypto-specific audit strategy; the model decides strategy while Flounder supplies sandbox, command policy, durable state, and reporting.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_541f2c766c9b30d0924308e8155dae2739710f46f440cb9ec5803133b8f17393","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_355f4f7b59726124cfd1d12db091a4de8c211c5f8ec590959b3fa30967ff0a6e"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The white-hat boundary forbids broadcasting transactions, moving funds, submitting writes, persisting access, or targeting systems outside the declared boundary; open-world confirmation is limited to fetch, search, fork, and read.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_755d4e61039b07d71f4dc4340f0e010907d883680488da0f4a9dffbc41ea021e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d7f2251affe89034d0b4e991b998b8792d8786ffd248753ca899afde793b6ec","slc_3e03864b117ed63cde7f512eed8180c214cd26b6866977b39e5bb0c0eb5cb1eb"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The tracked workflow runs prepare -> map -> dig -> synthesize -> verify -> confirm -> report, with each phase's purpose documented (e.g. Map enumerates and scores the audit surface without producing findings).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_77f15a067e4760369291d98862ba8f48c68e23086de29386187112d5ad7370e0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ef80bd5b505f9c5f51fb55e927e07424794d2eecf1b821810b9906a981fe56d9"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"Host execution is gated: `--sandbox-backend host --allow-host-execution` or FLOUNDER_ALLOW_HOST_EXECUTION=1 enables it, but host mode cannot enforce network sealing or kernel-level filesystem isolation and is not for untrusted targets.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_78e1d538ff4347db8e484a073c0e57ee0addbbf7b3a7ce206996f7dc21433806","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_00a60170e400e93b4f9d700873662589081bdf640511ad59c9dd53ad277e8244","slc_12696f0a714af486f7f0518e74143628dae0278f84890af743024c61b7136a8c"],"source_ids":["src_57c7248325f15442a1f02a4c54eff8f9","src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The product includes an Evaluations control plane for durable audit, benchmark, regression, and verification run groups, with lifecycle and evidence axes kept separate so a build failure cannot count as a safe control pass.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b3560f1a3f119e2ea1771326c211fdb718ebfdb9208d899fd87e00e87c6db1b9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f2c6c8fec3be60e954df805b2cf50949b22c60bd357ff422b3a322c0ce2abb16"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The product exposes a CLI with workflow verbs (prepare, run, map, audit, verify, confirm, report), a dashboard via `flounder ui`, a REST API where GET /api returns a self-describing catalog, and pi extension tools like flounder_prepare and flounder_run.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b9d00738b8440a3debae05969c6aeb71559d19ee52dec04b3e55224247806b0b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2858f639509c014bb70d6c6aba4d7f5d18574ad5a9938916c0266226a4d81c7e"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"Local state lives under ~/.flounder: a SQLite tracking database (flounder.db), per-run artifact directories, durable history/memory per target, a daemon workspace, and daemon-local provider auth.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf24230463cecc8d68dd3e029e3dcd63fc1a9fffcfa329a1b7bf283d82013982","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0f389b1181fcdd5dc7b65ca9c44986ae16175adf37fcca1eac6e599b5a468932","slc_2530bc4c589dddbd18704991c715282b728b1dfb7dd1ab0f68602df29d13eb3f"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"A daemon/control-plane split exists: remote daemons connect with minted tokens (`flounder server daemon-token mint`), providers are authenticated per executor machine, and projects pin to a daemon and provider profile.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e75e6dd772d3236c18b9cbe5b4354b303e7e9b7a23dc02c3aeb12fd2a053b174","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d5f6886e49f8ea58e8065cd4d71f2cc2138f70d24d46de15fabe6907048dc06b"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"Flounder is described as an autonomous white-hat security auditor providing security automation for target prep, audit, exploit construction, and execution proof.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fd77a43e868dfd2fadb6c290e738ebd6ff5e8b812bb485ff922dd847159121ae","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"adshao/flounder@6a5ee2313e0d snapshot 353ad75ef581bff8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_417992729ae1335a6eff828c15f325aab2e0c06154f2f1683e826b635b42059a"],"source_ids":["src_ac45032e236a5490a6b26fe328a0de98"],"text":"The default sandbox image is described as a baseline, not a promise to cover every target stack; specialized targets should supply a daemon- or operator-provided image with the exact toolchain.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:31:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b83851a680664610b448973151612e85"}
